de":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":38317240010},"loop_kind":"ci_fix","merge_base_sha":"c01ad62dd48a39f795fcb47fb481b9e26bcb296f","metadata":{"body":"Run one Weaver live check per package while the runner captures raw OTLP in a separate window for each scenario. Scenario assertions use those captures, and Weaver reports package-wide semantic convention violations.\n\nHTTP packages now point to an independent client or server contract:\n\n```yaml\n# client\nscenario_contract: ../../../../../../tools/http/contracts/client.yaml\nscenario_run: node scenario.js\n\n# server\nscenario_contract: ../../../../../../tools/http/contracts/server.yaml\nscenario_run: otel-http-drive --serve node ../server.js\n```\n\nA contract's `driver` sets the process lifecycle. `instrumentation` runs one process per action. `runner` keeps one measured server alive and drives its actions in order through the `jsonl-v1` protocol. Language helpers receive runner-selected actions as JSON instead of reading YAML.\n\n`expected_violations` now belongs at package level, where it reconciles with the aggregate Weaver report. Each pytest package item owns the full lifecycle, and diagnostic output contains per-scenario capture reports plus one aggregate Weaver report.\n","title":"Run one Weaver check per package with isolated OTLP capture"},"mode":"publish","pr":173,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1791844363,"generation":3,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"6cdd6719580243d5890b36c31a6eab00","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":["Analyze (actions)","CodeQL","Coverage model","Discover scenarios","EasyCLA","Lint","Relock (${{ matrix.ecosystem }})","Scenarios (database-java)","Scenarios (gen-ai-python)","Scenarios (http-dotnet)","Scenarios (http-go)","Scenarios (http-java)","Scenarios (http-js)","Scenarios (http-php)","Scenarios (http-python)","Scenarios (http-ruby-net_http-opentelemetry-instru